I am finally back in the flat.
I am very tired because I am sick.
I put on my pyjamas.
I really do not feel well.
I cough and my throat hurts.
Suddenly there is a knock at the door.
I open the door slowly.
Sabine is standing in the hallway.
She has a thermos in her hand.
"Hello Maya," says Sabine warmly.
"I am here because you are coughing so heavily."
She gives me the thermos.
"This is fresh ginger tea for you," she says.
"Thank you very much, Sabine," I answer quietly.
"The doctor says I should drink a lot of warm tea."
"Exactly," Sabine answers.
"You should just sleep now and rest."
She wishes me a good recovery and goes back into her flat.
I go to bed and pour myself a hot cup of tea.
